      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RING OF FIRE (3) dug deep to score a narrow victory at Wagga when sitting handy and fending off Hold This. He put in a strong rating there and now with the maiden out of the way, he looks ready to go on with the job. Well placed again here and he can bring up back-to-back wins. KURITHEA (7) is the clear danger, coming off a BM66 third at Taree where she was beaten just under a length as favourite, and her distance record of one win and one placing from two starts is a strong fit. Looks poised for a strong effort as she reaches her peak. COLORADO SUN (1) brings upside after charging over the top to win at Wagga in a change of tactics. Likely to get back again from the draw, but the mile looks a big tick for him and he'll be charging late in the race. ALABAMA CHARM (6) is better than he showed last time out when missing as favourite and getting to the mile looks a good move. ZIPPY LION (5) can repeat the dose after a nice win last start, with that race already producing 2 winners.",
